erry Hills Village.","ends":"2026-08-15T14:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Western Arapahoe, CO; Denver, CO; Douglas, CO; Jefferson, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.243371023415feaa4c3fe5781072da087af4c00f.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.243371023415feaa4c3fe5781072da087af4c00f.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Advisory","headline":"Flood Advisory issued August 15 at 1:26PM MDT until August 15 at 3:30PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Urban area and small stream flooding caused by excessive\nrainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...East Central Jefferson County in central Colorado...\nSouthwestern Arapahoe County in northeastern Colorado...\nExtreme Southwestern Denver County in northeastern Colorado...\nNorthwestern Douglas County in northeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 330 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\nWater over roadways.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 125 PM MDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges\nindicated heavy rain due to thunderstorms. This may cause urban\nand small stream flooding. Up to 0.5 inches of rain have fallen.\n\n- Additional rainfall amounts of 0.5 to 1 inch are expected over\nthe area. This additional rain will result in minor flooding.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nSouthern Lakewood, southwestern Centennial, Highlands Ranch,\nLittleton, southern Englewood, Greenwood Village, Sheridan,\nMorrison, Chatfield Reservoir, Red Rocks Park, Cherry Hills\nVillage, Columbine and Ken Caryl.","ends":"2026-08-15T15:30:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Arapahoe, CO; Denver, CO; Douglas, CO; Jefferson, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.01aaa824f71873e0eb66ad1b3c8f571bd84afcdc.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.01aaa824f71873e0eb66ad1b3c8f571bd84afcdc.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-15T19:12:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 151912 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion